  "tagline": "Seventy-one rooms and suites in a sandstone palace that is still a royal home.",
  "description": "Umaid Bhawan Palace is a golden sandstone palace above Jodhpur's old Blue City, set in 26 acres of gardens. It has 71 rooms and suites, and it is still a royal residence, with members of the family living in their own wing.\n\nThe palace is counted among the world's largest private homes. Its lobby rises under a 45-metre dome, and courtyards, arcades and the Baradari Lawns lie around it. Beneath the building is the Maharajah's subterranean Zodiac Pool, and there are also heated, indoor and outdoor pools. The palace has a museum, and champagne breakfasts are served on the Baradari Lawns.\n\nThe rooms are in the Art Deco style. Of the 71, 26 are rooms and 45 are suites, with views of the gardens, the pool, the city and Mehrangarh Fort. Palace Rooms measure 42 to 48 square metres. The Historical One Bedroom Suites, once the quarters of visiting royalty, run from 47 to 102 square metres, and the Royal and Grand Royal One Bedroom Suites from 111 to 130. At the top are three suites of several hundred square metres each: the Mehfil Suite at 400, the Maharaja Suite at 422 and the Maharani Suite at 450. Butler service and 24-hour in-room dining are available.\n\nPillars is an open-air cafe on a colonnaded terrace over the gardens and the city, serving breakfast from 7:30 am to 10:30 am. Risala serves Indian cooking, and the Trophy Bar is a sports-themed bar with finger food, open from 11:00 am to 11:00 pm. The kitchens draw on recipes handed down by royal chefs and on the European dishes the Maharajas brought home from their travels.\n\nJ Wellness Circle is the spa, offering Indian and international therapies. Beyond the grounds, the hotel arranges days at Mehrangarh Fort, Ghanta Ghar, Toorji Ka Jhalra Stepwell and the lake at Kaylana, and a royal welcome on arrival.\n\nThe palace suits travellers who want to stay in a royal home, with the airport only 15 minutes away by car. One small pet is allowed per room.",
